  "step_3": "The decision reason prioritizes the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, treating outcome differences as negligible. The individual’s report emphasizes the high probability of winning in Lottery A and appears to disregard the difference in outcome amounts between A and B. Despite numerical inaccuracies in the report (e.g., 95%, 40% higher), the core of the reasoning aligns with focusing on the probability of winning. The individual’s justification mirrors the rule of the decision reason: choose the lottery with the higher chance of a positive outcome. Although the exact numbers are misstated, the qualitative reasoning—favoring A due to its high and 'almost certain' win probability—matches the decision reason’s logic. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

